Point the crash window at the logs

When the program crashes, LibUltraShip's crash handler shows a window that asks the user to upload the logs to "the
support channel in discord", the wording of the project it comes from. A game built on LibUltraShip has no such
channel unless it sets one up, so the window sends its users somewhere that does not exist.

The window now says only to check the logs: LibUltraShip writes the crash report (the signal, the registers and the
stack) to logs/<name>.log beside the program (Context::InitLogging; patch 0011).

diff --git a/src/ship/debug/CrashHandler.cpp b/src/ship/debug/CrashHandler.cpp
index 63d5b071..8ec9014f 100644
--- a/src/ship/debug/CrashHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/ship/debug/CrashHandler.cpp
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@ static void ErrorHandler(int sig, siginfo_t* sigInfo, void* data) {
     }
     SDL_ShowSimpleMessageBox(
         SDL_MESSAGEBOX_ERROR, (GetCrashAppName() + " has crashed").c_str(),
-        (GetCrashAppName() + " has crashed. Please upload the logs to the support channel in discord.").c_str(),
+        (GetCrashAppName() + " has crashed. Please check the logs.").c_str(),
         nullptr);
     free(symbols);
     crashHandler->PrintCommon();
@@ -425,7 +425,7 @@ extern "C" LONG WINAPI seh_filter(PEXCEPTION_POINTERS ex) {
     WRITE_VAR_LINE(crashHandler, "Exception: ", exceptionString);
     crashHandler->PrintStack(ex->ContextRecord);
     MessageBoxA(nullptr,
-                (GetCrashAppName() + " has crashed. Please upload the logs to the support channel in discord.").c_str(),
+                (GetCrashAppName() + " has crashed. Please check the logs.").c_str(),
                 "Crash", MB_OK | MB_ICONERROR);
 
     return EXCEPTION_EXECUTE_HANDLER;
